---
import GraphDiagram from '@/components/GraphDiagram.astro';
import PropertyPackDiagramLegend from '@/components/property-pack/PropertyPackDiagramLegend.astro';
import PropertyPackPage from '@/components/property-pack/PropertyPackPage.astro';
import {
  boundaryDiagram,
  contexts,
  contextKindLabels,
  contextRoute,
  contextStats,
  contextMap,
} from '@/lib/property-pack-model.mjs';
---
<PropertyPackPage
  title="Contextual boundaries"
  description="The semantic homes of the Property Pack ontology candidate: six bounded contexts, a deliberately small common boundary and a machine-proposed DBT Smart Data scheme context."
  category="Model atlas"
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Contextual boundaries' }]}
>
  <h1>Contextual boundaries</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The candidate does not force every participant to use one universal meaning. Each
    resource belongs to one semantic home, while the Common boundary carries only meaning
    genuinely needed for exchange across several domains.
  </p>


  <h2 id="map">Boundary map</h2>
  <PropertyPackDiagramLegend variant="boundary" />
  <GraphDiagram
    source={boundaryDiagram()}
    minHeight="580px"
    caption="The arrows show shared elements supplied by the Common boundary. Cross-context mappings are a separate SKOS concern and no such mappings have yet been accepted."
  />

  <h2 id="homes">Contextual-boundary register</h2>
  <div class="v2-card-grid v2-context-card-grid">
    {contexts.map((context) => {
      const stats = contextStats(context.id);
      const title = context.id === 'dbt-smart-data'
        ? 'DBT Smart Data candidate semantic context'
        : context.label;
      return (
        <a class="v2-card v2-context-card" href={contextRoute(context)} aria-label={`Open ${title}`}>
          <p class="v2-context-card__field-label">Semantic home</p>
          <h3>{title}<code class="standalone-identifier">{context.id}</code></h3>
          <p class="v2-context-card__field-label">Kind</p>
          <p class="pill pill--info">{contextKindLabels[context.kind]}</p>
          <p class="v2-context-card__field-label">Definition</p>
          <p>{context.definition}</p>
          <dl class="v2-context-card__stats">
            <div><dt>OWL resources</dt><dd>{stats.resources}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Source data points</dt><dd>{stats.sourceItems}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Shapes</dt><dd>{stats.shapes}</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <span class="v2-card__action" aria-hidden="true">Open boundary →</span>
        </a>
      );
    })}
  </div>

  <h2 id="rules">Interpretation rules</h2>
  <div class="v2-note-grid">
    <section>
      <h3>One semantic home</h3>
      <p>{contextMap.rule}</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>Six bounded contexts</h3>
      <p>Conveyancing, Estate agency, Finance and banking, Property data services, Property technology, and Surveying and valuation own their internal meanings.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>DBT Smart Data is different</h3>
      <p>It is a machine-proposed semantic context for authorisation and controlled sharing—not the external DBT programme, an OPDA working-group decision or a property-domain bounded context.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>Mappings are a separate SKOS concern</h3>
      <p>The boundary arrows are not mappings. A reviewed correspondence may use an appropriate SKOS mapping predicate when both endpoints are SKOS concepts. SSSOM is not selected for internal cross-context records; it can be reconsidered only after the named external-use-case, consumer and Council gates. The register is currently empty and its status is <strong>{contextMap.mapping_status}</strong>. <a href="/semantic-modelling/evidence-and-mappings#cross-context-mappings">Read the Category 8 mapping method</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</PropertyPackPage>
